--- !u!114 &716443843
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 716443839}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9773422e06297d74eb8aabaa486dd9a6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  storyText: {fileID: 570073574}
  nextButton: {fileID: 596577239}
  previousButton: {fileID: 606786146}
  skipButton: {fileID: 566575110}
  audioSource: {fileID: 716443844}
  typingSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: eba50b361b24bac428dd3640754c47cf, type: 3}
  storyLines:
  - Kaelen, a scholar obsessed with mastering forbidden Void Magic, performed a ritual
    with the essence of a dying star, which backfired and destroyed his body. His
    soul merged with shadow, giving birth to the Dark King, a twisted figure cloaked
    in purple shadows. Wielding the cursed Shard of Starlight, he began his solitary
    reign over the forsaken realms.
  - "The Dark King, seeking only solitude, became a living curse, corrupting the
    lands around his fortress, Oblivion's Keep. His presence twisted nature\u2014plants
    blackened, animals became monstrous, and despair thickened the air. A spreading
    Void-born blight consumed Aethel, claiming all who dared approach, turning them
    into shadowy minions bound to his will."
  - As the blight consumed Aethel, its kingdoms fell into despair, their armies powerless
    against the shadow and its monstrous minions. Desperate rulers and elders turned
    to ancient prophecies foretelling a "Champion of Light" who would rise when the
    "Shadow swallowed the Star." With hope waning, they sent out a plea across the
    free lands, seeking anyone brave enough to confront the darkness and save Aethel.
  - From the hidden villages of the Sunken Forest, Elara, a young warrior attuned
    to light magic, rose to defend her people. When the blight threatened her homeland,
    she answered the call, wielding an ancient, glowing amulet. Braving corrupted
    beasts, treacherous lands, and spreading despair, she journeyed toward Oblivion's
    Keep, carrying the last flicker of hope against the encroaching darkness.
  - Elara reached the foreboding gates of Oblivion's Keep, where the air trembled
    with the agony of countless lost souls and the ground was slick with ancient
    blood. Inside, the Keep twisted into a nightmarish labyrinth, its halls littered
    with the bones and rusted armor of those who had failed the Dark King. Through
    shadow minions and the blight itself, he toyed with Elara, feeding on her fear
    and the fading light of hope she carried.
  - Deeper in the Keep, Elara entered a vast chamber paved with centuries of bones,
    polished by despair. At its center, the Dark King sat on a grotesque throne of
    petrified victims, his malevolent purple eyes fixed on her. Around him writhed
    the twisted husks of fallen heroes, once noble knights and mages, now silent
    puppets of his will, their suffering a crushing weight that pressed upon Elara.
  - "The Dark King\u2019s silent, soul-piercing laugh greeted Elara as he rose, the
    Shard of Starlight gleaming ominously against her amulet\u2019s glow. \u201CAnother
    fool,\u201D his voice whispered in her mind, \u201Canother soul for my collection.\u201D
    Moving with terrifying speed, he struck with pure malice, each blow carrying
    centuries of despair, aiming to crush her spirit long before her body, reveling
    in the slow extinguishing of defiance."
  - "The battle raged like a cruel dance of predator and prey. Elara struck with
    desperate bursts of light magic, yet the Dark King absorbed her attacks, each
    blow only fueling his power. His Shard of Starlight tore not just at her body,
    but at her spirit, flooding her mind with visions of fallen comrades, blighted
    lands, and hope turned to ash. Exhausted and faltering, her amulet\u2019s light
    flickered, as he waged war not merely against her, but against hope itself."
  - "With a final, desperate roar, Elara summoned all her light magic into a blinding
    nova. Though it could not destroy the Dark King, it briefly shattered his shadow,
    revealing the tormented scholar Kaelen beneath\u2014a soul trapped by his own
    ambition. Enraged, the Dark King struck with lethal force, the Shard of Starlight
    piercing Elara as her light faded, extinguishing the last hope of Aethel."
  - "With Elara\u2019s death, Aethel\u2019s final hope was extinguished. The blight
    devoured every tree and stream, twisting life into grotesque parodies, while
    the kingdoms fell into complete ruin. The Dark King returned to his throne, Elara\u2019s
    lifeless body joining his macabre collection, as he reigned supreme over a dead
    world\u2014an eternal monument to despair, ambition unchecked, and a night that
    would never end."
  backgroundImages:
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 640cd32e4c32a7640b2b73bdf6eeaf52, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 01be1df04f7c89441bac7d30a87906b7, type: 3}
